            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0696" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Gt. Brit/47</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Geddes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 29,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: With reference to the
                    Cabinet’s recent ruling against seizures outside the three-mile limit, except in
                    cases where the vessel concerned can be shown to have been in illegal
                    communication with the shore through her own boats, I should be most grateful if
                    you could inform me whether it is the intention to make this ruling
                    retrospective so as to apply to the case of vessels already seized.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. C. Geddes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
